# Build output
build/
build-*/
sdk/rust/target/
sdk/templates/rust/target/
sdk/rust/wasm/target/
sdk/templates/rust-wasm/target/
sdk/templates/rust-wasm/Cargo.lock
sdk/templates/rust/Cargo.lock
# Downloaded at configure time (FetchContent: WAMR, StormLib) into
# <build>/_deps, whatever the build folder is called; WAMR's old vendored path
_deps/
loader/third_party/wamr/core/
compile_commands.json
.cache/
__pycache__/

# Local editor configuration (machine-specific toolchain paths)
.clangd

# The Warcraft III files the tests read, a folder per version (input/1.27b/:
# input/README.md). Game files are Blizzard's and must never be committed.
# A version folder may also be a link to a game folder; only the README is kept.
/input
!/input/
/input/*
!/input/README.md
# Where the game's files went before input/ (older checkouts may still have it).
/WarCraft III/

# Defensive: game data, binaries and generated archives, in case a game folder
# or extracted files end up inside the repo under another name.
*.mpq
*.w3m
*.w3x
*.w3n
*.w3g
*.w3z
*.blp
*.mdx
*.mdl
*.tga
*.exe
*.dll
*.mix
*.ax
common.j
Blizzard.j
war3map.j

# Tome's runtime folders, if the repo root is ever used as a game folder
/mods/
/tome/
